<title>USA: TABLE - Overseas Shipholding Q2 shr rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Overseas Shipholding Q2 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>		     THREE MONTHS ENDED	  SIX MONTHS ENDED</p>
<p>			     JUNE 30,		    JUNE 30,</p>
<p>			 1997	  1996	  1997	  1996</p>
<p>Shipping</p>
<p> Revenues	  $122,801    $115,825     $250,594  $241,690</p>
<p>Net Income/</p>
<p>(Loss) (a)(b)</p>
<p>			  7,090	 3,101	  9,137     8,445</p>
<p>Net Income/</p>
<p> (Loss) Per Share     .19	   .08	    .25	 .23</p>
<p>Average Number</p>
<p>of Shares</p>
<p>Outstanding</p>
<p>			 36,280	36,234	 36,265    36,233</p>
<p>(a)  Gains from disposal of vessels were immaterial in the second quarter and first half of 1997.  Disposal of vessels in 1996 resulted in a loss, net of income tax, of $408,000 ($.01 per share) in the second quarter and a gain, net of income tax, of $4.482 million ($.12 per share) in the first half.</p>
<p>(b) Provisions for income taxes in 1997 were $2.76 million in the second quarter and $4.8 million in the first half. Provisions for income taxes in 1996 were $1.35 million in the second quarter and $5.6 million in the first half.</p>
<p>Full company name is Overseas Shipholding Group Inc.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
